            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0475" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7701: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-31T17:00:00-04:00">July 31, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>997. Your 1329, July 29 and Department’s 967, July 26. For Adler from the
                    Secretary of the Treasury. Re TF–144, July 29.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The day you receive this message you should submit your resignation as of
                        then.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The above information has been communicated to the British in Washington.
                        [Morgenthau.]</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
